# AAO provider activation TEMPLATE. Every value is intentionally EMPTY.
# Never commit a filled copy. The CEO (only) places real values on the host.
# Procedure: docs/procedures/PROVIDER_ACTIVATION_RUNBOOK.md
# Installed copies live under /etc/aao/ (0600, see runbook); this file is not read by any service.

# --- (a) Conversation provider: read by aao-api.service (/etc/aao/aao-api.env)
# --- and, only if turn recovery is enabled, aao-conversation-recovery.service (/etc/aao/aao-recovery.env).
# Must be exactly "openai-compatible"; anything else keeps the provider OFF.
AAO_CONVERSATION_PROVIDER=
# Full chat-completions endpoint, https only, no userinfo or query (e.g. https://HOST/v1/chat/completions).
AAO_CONVERSATION_API_URL=
# Model name as the provider spells it.
AAO_CONVERSATION_MODEL=
# SECRET. CEO places it directly on the host; never paste it in chat, tickets or PRs.
AAO_CONVERSATION_API_KEY=
# Recovery of expired turns; leave empty or "false" unless the CEO also activates the recovery worker.
AAO_CONVERSATION_RECOVERY_ENABLED=

# --- (b) Codex agent backend: AAO_AGENT_PROVIDER on the API (staging gate) AND on the Codex worker.
# Comma separated list of activated backends. "codex" activates it; empty keeps it OFF.
AAO_AGENT_PROVIDER=
# Worker only. Dedicated, isolated CODEX_HOME (never an operator ~/.codex). The path is not a secret;
# the auth.json inside is, and the CEO creates it with `codex login --device-auth`.
AAO_AGENT_CODEX_HOME=
# API only. Daily budget in USD; if empty there is NO limit (set it before activating).
AAO_AGENT_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=
# API only. Attempts per task; empty means the code default (3).
AAO_AGENT_MAX_ATTEMPTS=
